# Next.js / React UI

## App structure

- App Router only (`src/app`). No Pages Router.
- Use `'use client'` when the file needs state, effects, or browser APIs (see `@src/app/components/app-shell.tsx`, `@src/app/components/ui/navbar.tsx`, `@src/app/components/ui/chat-panel.tsx`).
- Put new UI under `src/app/components/ui/` (or `src/app/components/terminal/` for terminal-specific UI) unless introducing a clearer feature folder by request.
- Global shell lives in `@src/app/layout.tsx` → `@src/app/components/app-shell.tsx`: `ChatProvider` + `TerminalProvider` wrap every route, plus `ThemeBackground`, `Navbar`, and `LazyOverlays` (chat/terminal chunks load only after first open). Add new global overlays there, not in `page.tsx`. Do not reintroduce a global footer with duplicate contact/social links — those live in `ContactSection`.
- Home page (`@src/app/page.tsx`) composition: `Hero` → `SelectedWork` (`#work`) → `ExperienceTimeline` (`#experience`) → `SkillsGrid` (`#skills`) → `AboutSection` (`#about`) → `OutsideWork` → `ContactSection` (`#contact`).
- Project detail pages: `@src/app/projects/[slug]/page.tsx`, server-rendered from `@src/shared/projects.ts` with `generateStaticParams` + `generateMetadata`.
- Backend Route Handlers live under `src/app/api/v1/` (not in the UI tree); keep secrets and LLM/DB work out of client components.

## Styling

- Tailwind + existing shadcn primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `ScrollArea`).
- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` (`@src/lib/utils.ts`).
- Use themeable `surface-*` / `glow` tokens (`bg-surface-950`, `bg-surface-900/60` cards, mint `glow` accent). Never hardcode `zinc-*` or raw hex.
- Single dark look: `html.dark` plus `surface-*` / `glow` tokens in `@src/app/globals.css`. Ambient background is `@src/app/components/ui/theme-background.tsx`. Do not add album theme switching unless requested.
- Mono UI (terminal, commands, metrics) uses `font-mono` → JetBrains Mono via `--font-mono`.
- Use `ScrollArea` for dark-themed scroll regions; keep `color-scheme: dark` on `html`.
- Skill logos come from `@src/shared/skillIcons.ts` (inline path data). Never `import { … } from 'simple-icons'` — the package barrel is multi-MB and stalls SSR/dev compiles.
- `components.json` may alias utils to `@/app/lib/utils`; the real file is `@/lib/utils`. Do not duplicate `utils.ts` to “fix” the alias.
- Interactive targets should be at least 44px tall (chips, mobile menu buttons, terminal quick commands) for touch accessibility.

## State and exports

- Prefer local `useState` / `useRef` / `useEffect`. Two cross-cutting contexts exist: `ChatProvider` (`@src/app/components/ui/chat-provider.tsx`) and `TerminalProvider` (`@src/app/components/terminal/terminal-provider.tsx`). Don't add another global store unless justified.
- Chat thread state lives in `@src/hooks/useChatThread.ts` and is shared via `useChat()` so any section, the terminal, or project/experience buttons can call `sendMessage` / `openChat`.
- Match surrounding export style (named for hooks/primitives; default where the file already defaults; `fullscreen-terminal.tsx` default-exports for `next/dynamic`).

## Chat UX invariants

Canonical UI: `@src/app/components/ui/chat-panel.tsx` (fixed slide-over panel, full-width on mobile via `translate-x` + `w-full sm:max-w-md`). State/streaming: `@src/hooks/useChatThread.ts`.

- Render assistant markdown with `react-markdown` + `remark-gfm`
- Stream by appending content chunks to the assistant bubble
- Thread with `parent_id` / server `assistant_message_id`
- `useChat()` exposes `openChat({ context, prompt })` / `closeChat()` / `isOpen` / `context` (`{ type: 'project' | 'experience'; id }` or `null`), `error` + `retry()` for a failed send, and `clearChat()`
- Ctrl/Cmd+K clears the thread via `@src/hooks/refreshChatKeyHandler.ts`; the panel header also has an explicit clear button
- Autoscroll the message container (`scrollTop`), not the whole page (`scrollIntoView`)
- Contextual suggested prompts: general → `CHAT_SUGGESTIONS`, project → `getProjectSuggestions()`, experience → `getExperienceSuggestions()` (both in `@src/shared/`)
- Assistant replies may end with `[[LINK:project:<slug>]]` / `[[LINK:experience:<id>]]` markers (see `@src/lib/sourceLinks.ts`, mirrors `@src/lib/contactCta.ts`); render as clickable chips, never show the raw marker
- Do not call Telegram (or other side-effect notify APIs) after stream completion

## Terminal

- Engine (`@src/lib/terminal/`): `tokenizer.ts` → `parseCommand`, `registry.ts` (`registerCommand`/`getCommand`), `commands.ts` (all handlers, pure functions reading `@src/shared/` data), `index.ts` (`executeCommand`, the single entry point). Fully unit-tested under `tests/lib/terminal/`.
- New commands: add to `commands.ts` via `registerCommand`; return `{ kind: 'output' | 'clear' | 'action', segments, action? }` — never fetch or touch the DOM/router from a handler.
- UI (`@src/app/components/terminal/`): `terminal.tsx` is the single reusable core (history, arrow-key recall, Tab autocomplete, clickable command/suggestion chips) used by both `hero-terminal.tsx` (inline, hero) and `fullscreen-terminal.tsx` (overlay, opened via `useTerminal().open()`, lazy-loaded).
- Side effects (`scroll` / `navigate` / `open-chat`) are executed by `use-terminal-actions.ts`, not inside `terminal.tsx` — keeps the engine and rendering free of router/chat coupling.

## Profile content

- Client-facing copy, experience, skills, interests, nav links: `@src/shared/profile.ts`
- Project case studies: `@src/shared/projects.ts` (`PROJECTS`, `getProjectBySlug`); personal (non-work) projects may be flagged `placeholder: true` for draft content
- LLM background facts: `@src/server/ai/systemPrompt.ts` (the bot is Daniel's assistant; speak about him in the third person) — interpolates dates/roles/tech/impact from `profile.ts`/`projects.ts` via `@src/server/ai/context.ts` rather than duplicating them
- When updating jobs/education/location/projects, update `profile.ts`/`projects.ts` first; `systemPrompt.ts` picks up shared facts automatically, but review its hand-written narrative bullets too

## Resume

- Resume is a static asset at `/resume.pdf` (terminal `resume` command and contact section). Do not add a custom resume API route unless requested.
